      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to propagate exception to the other side of the binder you will need to try catch a RuntimeException here. (Same for every method)\n\nI think the quickest way to do so is like I did in aosp/1943964 with a public override calling the private same method without the receiver.\n```\n@Override\npublic registerBearer([...], AttributionSource source, SynchronousResultReceiver receiver) {\n Try {\n  registerBearer(token, callback, [...], source);\n  recevier.send(null);\n } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n  receiver.propagateException(e); // not throwing anything, but storing the exception in the receiver, it will be thrown when we will call `getValue(xxx)`\n }\n}\nprivate registerBearer([...], AttributionSource source) {\n  \u003cDo the Stuff for registerBearer\u003e\n}\n```",
